 ## Overview
-Scale Space Construction generates a continuous multi-scale representation of a scalar volume by solving the linear diffusion equation, producing a family of signals $L$ parameterized by scale $t$ [S1][S2, unofficial]. Unlike pyramid representations that subsample space and scale, this method avoids discretization artifacts in maxima detection by providing a continuous solution via Gaussian convolution [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Laplacian Grid Computation](3160-laplacian-grid-computation.md) by extending the Laplacian operator into a temporal diffusion process.
+Scale Space Construction generates a continuous multi-scale representation of a scalar volume by solving the linear diffusion equation, producing a family of signals $L$ parameterized by scale $t$ [S1][S2, unofficial]. Unlike pyramid representations that subsample space and scale, this method avoids discretization artifacts in maxima detection by providing a continuous solution via Gaussian convolution [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Laplacian Grid Computation](3160-laplacian-grid-computation.md) by extending the Laplacian operator into a temporal diffusion process [G].
 
